[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3393621217","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111379#issuecomment-3393621217","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111379","id":3393621217,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KRozh","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-11T19:50:07Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T18:36:02Z","body":"Having looked into this a little more, I think the problem isn't actually that the object is freed when the plugin is disabled (although, I still think that probably isn't ideal). The errors and crashes only happen specifically when the plugin *enables* itself again. I strongly suspect it's a similar case to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100750, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102535, because always using `CACHE_MODE_REUSE` when loading addon scripts seems to avoid the issue.\n\nThe same issue can be reproduced by any script calling the following from anywhere:\n\n`ResourceLoader.load(get_script().resource_path, \"\", ResourceLoad